Cell["\<\
Now, use this steady state value of B in the ODE\[CloseCurlyQuote]s. This is \
always valid if we are seeking steady-state solutions to the system. We do \
this because it clarifies that \[Alpha], \[Xi], and \[Delta] can be combined \
into a single composite parameter. This reduces the number of model \
parameters by 2. We now need only \[ScriptCapitalA] rather than \[Xi], \
\[Alpha], and \[Delta]. Below, we run a numerical check to make sure the \
book-keeping is accurate.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965419405859036*^9, 3.965419421318761*^9}, {
  3.965419929168708*^9, 3.965419986481385*^9}, {3.970775040859836*^9, 
  3.970775183335005*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d89643ab-c16d-49ca-8efa-\
f62f4dc578d7"],

